WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.080
Special planting days were recently held at
Silverstream Reserve as part of

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.740
Matariki Tu Rākau.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:20.320
Local members of the RSA, joined with Council
Staff, Te Uru Rākau Forestry New Zealand,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:26.120
the Silverstream Reserve Advisory Group and
other volunteers to plant 660 Kanuka seedlings

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.800
over two days.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.360
Matariki Tu Rākau is a partnership between
Te Uru Rākau - Forestry New Zealand, and local

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.150
communities to plant trees to recognise the
service of men and women of the New Zealand

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:53.129
Defence Forces and mark the 100-year anniversary
of the end of the First World War.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:59.200
It’s part of a wider government initiative
to plant one billion trees over the next 10 years.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.120
The trees have been planted in a grid 
to represent soldiers standing in formation.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:12.480
In the future, seating will be installed to
create a beautiful space to sit and reflect.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.429
The plantings are just one small part of the
Silverstream Reserve restoration project,

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:22.729
which aims to return approximately 52 hectares
to native planting over the coming decades.

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:29.680
In just the next year alone, volunteers and
the Council are hoping to plant 2000 additional trees.

